{"seed":{"mim":"616482","entry_type":"phenotype","prefix":"#","title":"ACHONDROPLASIA, SEVERE, WITH DEVELOPMENTAL DELAY AND ACANTHOSIS NIGRICANS","alt_titles":[],"symbol":"SADDAN","gene_symbols":[],"seed_pmids":[],"max_year":2008},"nodes":[{"id":"entry","type":"Entry","label":"ACHONDROPLASIA, SEVERE, WITH DEVELOPMENTAL DELAY AND ACANTHOSIS NIGRICANS","mim":"616482","entry_type":"phenotype"},{"id":"section:description","type":"Section","label":"description"},{"id":"section:nomenclature","type":"Section","label":"nomenclature"},{"id":"section:cloning_expression","type":"Section","label":"cloning_expression"},{"id":"section:gene_structure","type":"Section","label":"gene_structure"},{"id":"section:clinical_features","type":"Section","label":"clinical_features"},{"id":"section:other_features","type":"Section","label":"other_features"},{"id":"section:biochemical_features","type":"Section","label":"biochemical_features"},{"id":"section:inheritance","type":"Section","label":"inheritance"},{"id":"section:cytogenetics","type":"Section","label":"cytogenetics"},{"id":"section:mapping","type":"Section","label":"mapping"},{"id":"section:heterogeneity","type":"Section","label":"heterogeneity"},{"id":"section:gene_function","type":"Section","label":"gene_function"},{"id":"section:molecular_genetics","type":"Section","label":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"section:genotype_phenotype_correlations","type":"Section","label":"genotype_phenotype_correlations"},{"id":"section:pathogenesis","type":"Section","label":"pathogenesis"},{"id":"section:diagnosis","type":"Section","label":"diagnosis"},{"id":"section:clinical_management","type":"Section","label":"clinical_management"},{"id":"section:population_genetics","type":"Section","label":"population_genetics"},{"id":"section:evolution","type":"Section","label":"evolution"},{"id":"section:animal_model","type":"Section","label":"animal_model"},{"id":"section:history","type":"Section","label":"history"},{"id":"paper:18076102","type":"Paper","label":"Zankl et al. (2008)","pmid":"18076102","year":2008,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Prenatal and postnatal presentation of severe achondroplasia with developmental delay and acanthosis nigricans (SADDAN) due to the FGFR3 Lys650Met mutation."},{"id":"paper:11406607","type":"Paper","label":"Iwata et al. (2001)","pmid":"11406607","year":2001,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"supporting","title":"Highly activated Fgfr3 with the K644M mutation causes prolonged survival in severe dwarf mice."},{"id":"paper:10377013","type":"Paper","label":"Bellus et al. (1999)","pmid":"10377013","year":1999,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"Severe achondroplasia with developmental delay and acanthosis nigricans (SADDAN): phenotypic analysis of a new skeletal dysplasia caused by a Lys650Met mutation in fibroblast growth factor receptor 3."},{"id":"paper:10053006","type":"Paper","label":"Tavormina et al. (1999)","pmid":"10053006","year":1999,"content_level":"abstract","relevance":"primary","title":"A novel skeletal dysplasia with developmental delay and acanthosis nigricans is caused by a Lys650Met mutation in the fibroblast growth factor receptor 3 gene."},{"id":"finding:10053006:1","type":"Finding","label":"Tavormina et al. (1999) described 4 unrelated individuals with a skeletal dysplasia nearly as severe as thanatophoric dysplasia type I. Three of the 4 developed extensive acanthosis nigricans starting in early childhood and had severe neurologic impairment. All of them survived past infancy without prolonged life support.","pmid":"10053006","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"gene:FGFR3","type":"Gene","label":"FGFR3"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000924","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormality of the skeletal system","hpo_id":"HP:0000924"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000956","type":"Phenotype","label":"Acanthosis nigricans","hpo_id":"HP:0000956"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0012758","type":"Phenotype","label":"Neurodevelopmental delay","hpo_id":"HP:0012758"},{"id":"finding:10053006:2","type":"Finding","label":"Tavormina et al. (1999) named the phenotype caused by the FGFR3 Lys650Met mutation 'severe achondroplasia with developmental delay and acanthosis nigricans' (SADDAN). They chose a separate name because the phenotype differs significantly from those of other known FGFR3 mutations.","pmid":"10053006","section":"nomenclature"},{"id":"finding:10053006:3","type":"Finding","label":"Tavormina et al. (1999) found the same FGFR3 missense mutation, A1949T (Lys650Met), in all 4 unrelated individuals with SADDAN. The change is at the nucleotide next to the thanatophoric dysplasia type II mutation (A1948G; Lys650Glu). It produces a different amino acid substitution at a highly conserved codon in the activation loop of the kinase domain.","pmid":"10053006","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"variant:FGFR3:c.1949A>T","type":"Variant","label":"FGFR3 c.1949A>T / p.A1949T / p.K650M","gene":"FGFR3","keys":["c.1949A>T","p.A1949T","p.K650M"],"omim_name":"FGFR3, ALA1949THR"},{"id":"finding:10053006:4","type":"Finding","label":"In transient transfection studies by Tavormina et al. (1999), the FGFR3 Lys650Met mutation caused a dramatic increase in constitutive receptor kinase activity. The activity was about 3 times higher than with the thanatophoric dysplasia type II mutation Lys650Glu.","pmid":"10053006","section":"gene_function"},{"id":"finding:10377013:1","type":"Finding","label":"Bellus et al. (1999) gave a detailed clinical account of the SADDAN phenotype. The FGFR3 Lys650Met mutation caused severe disturbances of endochondral bone growth that approached and overlapped those seen in thanatophoric dysplasia type I, but was most often compatible with survival into adulthood. Some patients had unusual bone deformities such as femoral bowing with reverse (posterior apex) tibial and fibular bowing and 'ram's horn' bowing of the clavicle. Surviving patients had progressive acanthosis nigricans, structural anomalies of the central nervous system, seizures, and severe developmental delay.","pmid":"10377013","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002652","type":"Phenotype","label":"Skeletal dysplasia","hpo_id":"HP:0002652"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002979","type":"Phenotype","label":"Bowing of the legs","hpo_id":"HP:0002979"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002982","type":"Phenotype","label":"Tibial bowing","hpo_id":"HP:0002982"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0000889","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormal clavicle morphology","hpo_id":"HP:0000889"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0012443","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormal brain morphology","hpo_id":"HP:0012443"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001250","type":"Phenotype","label":"Seizure","hpo_id":"HP:0001250"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0011344","type":"Phenotype","label":"Severe global developmental delay","hpo_id":"HP:0011344"},{"id":"finding:10377013:2","type":"Finding","label":"Bellus et al. (1999) noted that although the Lys650Met mutation lies in the same FGFR3 codon as the thanatophoric dysplasia type II mutation (Lys650Glu) and has a similar effect on constitutive activation of the FGFR3 tyrosine kinase, it is not associated with cloverleaf skull or craniosynostosis.","pmid":"10377013","section":"genotype_phenotype_correlations"},{"id":"variant:FGFR3:p.K650E","type":"Variant","label":"FGFR3 p.K650E","gene":"FGFR3","keys":["p.K650E"],"omim_name":"FGFR3, LYS650GLU"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002676","type":"Phenotype","label":"Cloverleaf skull","hpo_id":"HP:0002676"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0001363","type":"Phenotype","label":"Craniosynostosis","hpo_id":"HP:0001363"},{"id":"finding:10377013:3","type":"Finding","label":"Bellus et al. (1999) noted that they had previously identified a novel missense mutation, Lys650Met, in the tyrosine kinase domain of FGFR3 in 4 unrelated individuals with the condition they called SADDAN.","pmid":"10377013","section":"molecular_genetics"},{"id":"finding:11406607:1","type":"Finding","label":"To determine whether the FGFR3 K650M mutation causes the SADDAN phenotype, Iwata et al. (2001) introduced the corresponding point mutation (K644M) into the mouse Fgfr3 gene. Heterozygous mutant mice had a phenotype similar to human SADDAN, and most survived the perinatal period. The authors suggested that the survival of SADDAN patients is indeed due to the K650M mutation. Long bone abnormalities in the SADDAN mice were milder than in the TDII mouse model, and the rib cartilage, trachea and nasal septum showed overgrowth of cartilaginous tissue.","pmid":"11406607","section":"animal_model"},{"id":"variant:FGFR3:p.K644M","type":"Variant","label":"FGFR3 p.K644M","gene":"FGFR3","keys":["p.K644M"],"omim_name":"FGFR3, LYS644MET"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0011314","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormal long bone morphology","hpo_id":"HP:0011314"},{"id":"hpo:HP:0002763","type":"Phenotype","label":"Abnormal cartilage morphology","hpo_id":"HP:0002763"},{"id":"inh:AD","type":"Inheritance","label":"Autosomal dominant","hpo_id":"HP:0000006"},{"id":"finding:11406607:2","type":"Finding","label":"Iwata et al. (2001) noted that FGFR3 carrying the SADDAN mutation (K650M) is more activated in vitro than FGFR3 carrying the TDII mutation (K650E), yet TDII is lethal at birth while most SADDAN patients survive. In primary chondrocyte cultures, a low concentration of FGF ligand activated MAP kinase differently in cells from wildtype and SADDAN mice.","pmid":"11406607","section":"pathogenesis"},{"id":"finding:18076102:1","type":"Finding","label":"Zankl et al. (2008) described the prenatal and postnatal features of a patient with SADDAN. The case confirmed the severe morbidity of SADDAN and added to the reports of early mortality associated with the disorder. The authors also reviewed the clinical and radiologic characteristics of all reported cases of SADDAN.","pmid":"18076102","section":"clinical_features"},{"id":"phenotext:early mortality","type":"PhenotypeText","label":"early mortality"},{"id":"finding:18076102:2","type":"Finding","label":"In a patient with SADDAN, Zankl et al. (2008) confirmed the clinical diagnosis by identifying the FGFR3 Lys650Met mutation through mutation analysis. They noted this was one of only six SADDAN cases with molecular analysis reported in the literature.","pmid":"18076102","section":"molecular_genetics"}],"edges":[{"src":"paper:10053006","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:10053006:1"},{"src":"finding:10053006:1","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:clinical_features"},{"src":"finding:10053006:1","rel":"mentions_gene","dst":"gene:FGFR3","pmid":"10053006"},{"src":"finding:10053006:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0000924","pmid":"10053006","present":true,"frequency":"4/4","text":"severe skeletal dysplasia"},{"src":"finding:10053006:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0000956","pmid":"10053006","present":true,"frequency":"3/4","text":"acanthosis nigricans"},{"src":"finding:10053006:1","rel":"has_phenotype","dst":"hpo:HP:0012758","pmid":"10053006","present":true,"frequency":"3/4","text":"severe neurological impairment"},{"src":"paper:10053006","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:10053006:2"},{"src":"finding:10053006:2","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:nomenclature"},{"src":"finding:10053006:2","rel":"mentions_gene","dst":"gene:FGFR3","pmid":"10053006"},{"src":"paper:10053006","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:10053006:3"},{"src":"finding:10053006:3","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:molecular_genetics"},{"src":"finding:10053006:3","rel":"mentions_gene","dst":"gene:FGFR3","pmid":"10053006"},{"src":"finding:10053006:3","rel":"reports_variant","dst":"variant:FGFR3:c.1949A>T","pmid":"10053006","zygosity":"unknown","origin":"unknown","as_reported":"A1949T: Lys650Met"},{"src":"variant:FGFR3:c.1949A>T","rel":"in_gene","dst":"gene:FGFR3"},{"src":"paper:10053006","rel":"reports","dst":"finding:10053006:4"},{"src":"finding:10053006:4","rel":"in_section","dst":"section:gene_function"},{"src":"finding:10053006:4","rel":"mentions_gene","dst":"gene:FGFR3","pmid":"10053006"},{"src":"finding:10053006:4","rel":"reports_variant","dst":"variant:FGFR3:c.1949A>T","pmid":"10053006","zygo